-- title:
--   Divisor-string modules are cyclic with one-dimensional joint eigenspaces
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a nonzero natural number and let $V$ be a finite-dimensional complex vector space (with the usual additive group and module structures). Let $e : \mathbb{N} \to V$ be a family of vectors whose restriction to the divisors of $D$, i.e. $(e_d)_{d \mid D}$, is linearly independent over $\mathbb{C}$ and spans $V$, so that it is a basis indexed by $\mathrm{Nat.divisors}\ D$. Let $U : \mathbb{N} \to \mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}} V$ be a family of endomorphisms such that: $U_p$ and $U_q$ commute for all primes $p, q$ dividing $D$; for every prime $q \mid D$ and every $d \mid D$ with $q \mid d$ one has $U_q(e_d) = e_{d/q}$; and for every prime $q \mid D$ there exist scalars $a, b \in \mathbb{C}$ (depending on $q$ only) with $U_q(e_d) = a \cdot e_d + b \cdot e_{dq}$ for all $d \mid D$ with $q \nmid d$. The conclusion is twofold. First, for every $d \mid D$ there is an element $T$ of the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}} V$ generated by $\{A : A = U_q \text{ for some prime } q \mid D\}$ with $e_d = T(e_D)$; in particular $V$ is a cyclic module over that subalgebra, generated by $e_D$. Second, for every function $\mathrm{lam} : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{C}$, the intersection over the prime factors $q$ of $D$ of the eigenspaces of $U_q$ for the eigenvalue $\mathrm{lam}(q)$ has $\mathbb{C}$-dimension at most $1$.
--
--   This is the linear algebra underlying multiplicity one for the operators $U_q$ on the space spanned by the degeneracy translates $g(d\tau)$, $d \mid D$, of a fixed form of lower level: such a "divisor string" basis makes the space cyclic over the algebra generated by the $U_q$, whence joint eigenspaces are lines. It is used in [`CuspForm.nonempty_basis_fin_one_gammaH_and_finrank_eigenspace_eq_one`](thm.html#CuspForm.nonempty_basis_fin_one_gammaH_and_finrank_eigenspace_eq_one) to pin down one-dimensionality of the relevant eigenspace of cusp forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Module_End_mem_span_prod_apply_and_finrank_iInf_eigenspace_le_one_of_divisorString.lean

